WEBVTT

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:19.080
This is for the best,

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.580
right, everyone?

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.260
Mobius has begun to collapse.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:39.010
μ is disoriented, and she can't 
control the world anymore.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.030
You seem different.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:20.950
I've regained my powers and memories.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:26.160
Which also proves that 
μ is in terrible shape.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:29.310
But your body hasn't been restored.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:31.450
Jeez, you had to say that?

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:32.310
What about you, Ritsu?

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.130
I've remembered.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:39.820
That it might be my fault 
μ ended up that way.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:50.350
Back in reality, I could never 
socialize well with others.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:55.720
I could go days before realizing 
something was wrong with my throat,

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.260
because I didn't speak to others.

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:03.490
I was like a decorative plant 
in the corner of the room,

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:06.540
just living without anyone noticing.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:11.180
Then one day I heard μ's voice.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.790
It was the first time I felt 
connected to someone else.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:18.510
μ would happily listen to me talk.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.820
She answered kindly.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:24.030
I felt as if the words I could 
never share with others

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:26.340
were able to reach μ alone.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:32.730
It's difficult, isn't it? 
Putting your thoughts into words.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:37.020
Hey, why did you return 
to reality by yourself?

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:42.570
I didn't know how to explain 
things about me and μ.

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:46.000
Besides, this is something only I can do.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.040
Something I have to do.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.350
Ritsu...

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:53.750
I wasn't able to stop μ in the end.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.960
I want to make everyone happy!

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:00.050
Hey, Ritsu? What should I do?

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.320
I couldn't give her a proper answer.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:05.400
Don't worry!

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.390
Whatever your wish, I'll grant it!

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:10.230
With my songs!

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.020
In that case,

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.250
this time you need to confront μ

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:21.030
and tell her how you feel.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:23.670
I'm sure it'll reach μ!

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:24.530
Yeah.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:27.800
So Ritsu, please take care of μ.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:35.000
If this keeps up and Mobius is destroyed, 
will we be able to go home?

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.000
You think we will?

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.250
If that's true, then we can just stay here.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.510
Have you forgotten what happened to Yamada?!

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:46.390
If this place goes away, we vanish with it.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:50.010
I'm the only one

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:53.860
who hasn't spoken about my real self, right?

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:57.960
You see, I'm a single mother.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:00.760
My child's name is Tak-kun.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:06.780
Back there, I've never done a single 
motherly thing for my child.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:11.790
Even though he's my child, 
I resented him at times.

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:15.260
I really regret it now.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.490
He might not ever forgive me.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:22.670
But I have to go home to reality

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:24.170
and give Tak-kun another hug!

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:29.430
You're all so annoying!

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:32.430
I'll send you all to Heaven!

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:36.440
Man, I think your Heaven's in trouble here.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.810
Be quiet! Enough nonsense!

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:42.570
We'll save this world from its crisis!

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:47.530
We need to run soon, too.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.160
Huh?! To where?!

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:52.320
There's no save point here for us!

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:54.540
At this rate, we're all going to disappear.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:58.200
Once we defeat those of you 
rejecting μ, rejecting this world,

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.350
the distortion in this world will be fixed!

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:01.540
We won't let it end!

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:05.510
That's right! We won't let it end here.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:08.260
We're going back!

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:12.890
We're all alike.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.830
We all have something 
we refuse to surrender.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:20.730
What's different is only whether reality

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:24.190
or Mobius is what affirms us.

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:30.070
We're going back to reality 
to live our lives!

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:51.020
Everyone's pain!

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:04.430
<i>This scenery plastered with kind lies,</i>

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:06.690
You're going to face the sins 
you've committed in reality?

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:06.690
<i>and a daily life continuing forever</i>

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:08.880
<i>carries the absurdity of reality</i>

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:09.400
Your sins won't go away.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:11.200
<i>away to a far, far away world.</i>

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:13.360
Ichika will never forgive you.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.360
<i>My love for you</i>

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:15.520
<i>is enough to drive me.</i>

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:16.950
So you'll never be able to escape 
your suffering while you live.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:17.880
<i>My hate for you</i>

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:18.910
Drop dead, Shogo.

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:20.110
<i>is enough to make me ache.</i>

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.540
Are you Natsume Asuka?

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:22.540
<i>Some might say this is all fake,</i>

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.570
<i>but if it heals this grief away,</i>

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:26.700
<i>I'll become dependent on 
its continued deception.</i>

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:28.520
Natsume, why... are you... in here?

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:29.320
<i>See? It doesn't hurt anymore.</i>

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:33.340
Why did Ichika choose to die 
with you instead of me?

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:31.500
<i>My urge to love you</i>

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.590
<i>is more priceless than anything</i>

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:37.530
If she had chosen me, I could have 
passed on with her at the end.

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:35.980
<i>My urge to hate you</i>

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:37.640
<i>is more unbearable than anything.</i>

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:45.320
<i>This is an endless Mobius strip.</i>

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:39.390
So then,

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:42.560
why did she choose a coward like you?

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:43.340
Why?

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:44.650
Why?

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:47.710
And then there's you!

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:50.280
<i>So why do you want to run away?</i>

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:49.950
After walking all over her feelings,

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:52.650
you let her die all by herself!

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:56.280
<i>When all the happiness in the world is here?</i>

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:58.040
<i>She smiles...</i>

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:02.410
<i>A world without you, 
without you, without you...</i>

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:03.040
Shogo, you understand, don't you?

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:07.180
<i>I won't accept it. I won't accept it!
 See, you're here, aren't you?</i>

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:06.540
Ichika is still alive.

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:10.440
I can't tolerate a world without Ichika.

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:10.410
<i>As long as you're here, as long as 
you're here, as long as you're here...</i>

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:11.630
<i>I don't need anything else.</i>

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:12.960
But she's in here.

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:17.310
<i>May this miniature garden 
where you smile last forever.</i>

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:15.680
Even now, she's by my side.

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:19.260
I won't let anyone interfere 
with our happiness!

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:23.850
I know I ran!

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:24.800
I was scared.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:26.920
I didn't know what to do.

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:28.320
That's why I came to this world.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:33.200
No, no! I'm the one who invited you here!

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.110
That has to be the truth!

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:37.290
<i>Our peaceful days are eroding away,</i>

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:39.390
<i>and you can't just ignore it.</i>

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:41.330
Drop dead, Shogo!

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:41.720
<i>Why are you rejecting happiness?</i>

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:43.920
<i>You could just stay and wait here.</i>

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:48.170
You will never find peace for all eternity!

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:52.920
Besides, what can a coward 
like you possibly do

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:54.220
when you return to reality?!

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:55.130
<i>Even if it's distorted...</i>

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:56.130
There's no place for you there!

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:57.600
<i>Even if it's rotten...</i>

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:58.640
Mobius is finished, too.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:59.820
<i>Even if it's stagnant...</i>

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.450
Even μ can't fully support it anymore.

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:01.320
<i>It's still happiness.</i>

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:08.260
<i>What do you hope to accomplish 
by finding an end?</i>

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:05.350
She's endured well, considering that delicate body.

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:10.600
I wasn't able to be closest to 
Ichika when her time came,

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:19.740
<i>You don't want to go back to horrible form 
spreading resentment everywhere, do you?</i>

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:12.570
but this time it's different.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:14.490
This time!

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:20.990
So let's enjoy these final moments, Shogo.

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:21.770
<i>She's ticked...</i>

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:26.220
<i>A world without you, 
without you, without you...</i>

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:30.920
<i>Never existed...
 Never existed from the start.</i>

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:30.920
Satake!

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:34.170
<i>You're not here... You're not here...
 You're not here,</i>

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:34.760
Farewell, Shogo.

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.420
<i>Shut up!</i>

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:38.890
<i>I'll stab a knife into that 
persistent buzz again today! {Lyric cut halfway}</i>

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:42.760
Ritsu...

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:45.480
President!

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:47.290
You're okay!

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:49.260
Jeez! Where did you go?!

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:51.570
I thought you betrayed us!

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:54.530
Sorry, everyone.

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:57.160
You came back?

00:09:57.720 --> 00:09:58.700
Yeah.

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:03.370
There are still things 
I need to do in this world.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:03.990
<b>Destroy your ideals and self, 
and return to hell and reality.</b>

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:08.960
<i>Oh, wandering heart,</i>

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:10.420
Things you need to do?

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:13.840
<i>forget about everything,</i>

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:12.380
What can you possibly do?

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:15.130
Can't you hear it?

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:25.770
<i>view only your ideals in this 
world guided by this song.</i>

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:19.340
The dying screams of Mobius, 
μ's song of demise?

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:28.360
It's over. All of it.

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:30.230
Along with Mobius.

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:32.240
I'll take everyone's unhappiness.

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:35.560
<i>It was so painful, wasn't it?</i>

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:34.690
...and I'll turn it into song.

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:37.400
Lament, sorrow...

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:40.330
<i>It was so sad, wasn't it?</i>

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:39.490
hatred, all of it...

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:41.860
I'll accept it for you!

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:49.880
<i>I'll accept it in place of your tears.</i>

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:54.650
<i>What do you seek?</i>

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:59.470
<i>What do you wish to become?</i>

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:59.160
H-Hey, Thorn?

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:00.300
What are you doing?

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:03.970
<i>I'll grant your wish,</i>

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:10.060
<i>so tell me.</i>

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:12.720
<i>CRY!</i>

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:15.700
<i>I can't not scream!</i>

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:18.060
<i>I can't not sing!</i>

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:17.280
No way!

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:24.070
<i>I'll scoop up your words 
as they wilt away, so</i>

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:25.420
Komori-kun!

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:31.480
<i>Cry! As if you're screaming, 
as if you're singing,</i>

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:28.520
We're going to eat lunch
 together, right, Suzuna?

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:32.980
N-No!

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:40.420
<i>in this never ending, always 
repeating, Shangri-La.</i>

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:48.100
Shogo!

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:51.600
Natsume, give up already.

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:00.620
N-No way...

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:11.660
μ...

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:13.290
Oh crap!

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:16.880
Save me, μ!

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:19.760
Hey, μ! What's happened to you?!

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:22.220
It's all right.

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:25.430
You won't have to suffer anymore.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:30.600
I'm going to make you all happy.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.390
Inside me!

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:39.730
Aria!

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:45.940
Go alive!

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:51.900
Natsume, you're right.

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:53.540
My sin will never go away.

00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:56.760
But even so, I have to face it.

00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:00.700
In reality, not here in Mobius.

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:07.690
I don't want to live in 
a world without Ichika.

00:13:11.460 --> 00:13:13.230
I'm leaving the rest to you!

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:15.740
Yeah, I know.

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:18.300
Ritsu, make sure to tell her!

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:21.440
Reach μ's heart!

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:29.300
μ, can you hear me?

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:33.800
It's just the two of us now.

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:35.460
That was how it started.

00:13:35.970 --> 00:13:40.340
Back then, I really just 
spoke to you for no reason.

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:44.300
I never even imagined that 
you would respond back.

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:46.680
So I was really surprised

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:48.730
and spilled my coffee.

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:53.690
That's why my first memories 
of you smell like coffee.

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:57.610
We chatted about a lot of things, didn't we?

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:03.220
Like how I found a kitten abandoned 
in a park on my way to work,

00:14:03.220 --> 00:14:05.190
but I couldn't take it in.

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:10.240
I was still worried about it, so I 
went back to the park during lunch,

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:11.910
but the kitten was gone.

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:15.560
When I was upset with regret, you spoke to me.

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:19.080
You said, "It's all right."

00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:23.560
Those words really saved me.

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:27.360
But I imagine you probably didn't really know

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:29.930
whether that kitten was all right.

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:35.430
Your words were simply 
what I wanted to hear most.

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:46.360
μ...

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:52.570
You asked me what happiness is, right?

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:55.850
Back in reality, and even in here,

00:14:55.850 --> 00:15:00.040
I couldn't give you a proper answer.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:04.280
So let's talk about happiness once more.

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:12.220
μ, I...

00:15:12.690 --> 00:15:17.720
always wanted someone to listen my thoughts.

00:15:18.340 --> 00:15:22.560
Yet despite that, I didn't want to let anyone,
 even you, get too close to me.

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:26.620
I kept that darkness constantly 
hidden in my heart.

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:32.190
Here in Mobius, I borrowed my coworker's 
words to desperately hide that,

00:15:32.190 --> 00:15:33.990
and I continued to fake who I was.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:40.410
That's why I've never been able 
to tell you what I truly feel.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:44.670
The old me...

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:47.340
No, even now,

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:51.470
I'm constantly longing for 
others to understand me.

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:57.890
But I know that's a dream 
that'll never come true.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:02.180
So I debate about it, 
agonize over it, and struggle.

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:05.920
In other words, even in this world,

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:08.650
I can't say I'm happy yet.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:09.690
But that's because...

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:26.310
But μ, that's because we're wrong.

00:16:27.530 --> 00:16:31.690
It's probably impossible for others 
to understand a person completely.

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:33.980
Sadly enough.

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:38.640
But everyone wants to be closer to others,

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:41.070
so they try learning psychology;

00:16:41.070 --> 00:16:43.340
they try expressing themselves online;

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:46.360
they try to find answers in stories;

00:16:46.790 --> 00:16:48.660
they try all kinds of different things.

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:53.030
Because it's lonely being on your own.

00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:56.300
Because you want someone to understand you.

00:16:56.900 --> 00:17:01.200
True happiness is something...

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:04.540
Something that people 
search out for themselves

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:07.060
in their own ways.

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:10.170
It's not something that can 
ever be granted by another.

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:13.920
Words are hard.

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:16.550
You can like and hate the same thing.

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:21.720
Weakness also exists within strength.

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:26.850
Painful wounds of the body are different 
from painful wounds of the heart.

00:17:27.490 --> 00:17:29.940
And wounds themselves have 
many different meanings as well.

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:33.040
Even the word "happiness"

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:35.920
has a different meaning to every person.

00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:45.290
So my happiness is...

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:57.130
When I came here and got involved 
with everyone in the Go-Home Club,

00:17:57.680 --> 00:18:00.380
it was difficult prying into them.

00:18:00.380 --> 00:18:04.220
I imagine that was likely 
someone else's role.

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:05.600
But even so!

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:08.310
I wanted to understand them!

00:18:16.130 --> 00:18:20.820
μ, what was going through your 
mind as you created Mobius?

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:23.080
How strongly have you longed for happiness?

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:29.350
Maybe my words aren't reaching you.

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:31.790
But I'll keep telling you!

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:34.250
This time I won't make that mistake!

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:37.780
I'll tell you with my very own words!

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:44.090
It's strange.

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:47.850
Everyone in the Go-Home 
Club wants to go home,

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:50.560
but they're also a little 
afraid of going back.

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:54.400
The Musicians supposedly 
want to stay in this world,

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:57.030
but occasionally they look lonely.

00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:59.020
White and black.

00:18:59.020 --> 00:19:00.840
It's strange and complicated.

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:04.570
That's how the human mind is.

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:10.250
We long for our own happiness, 
while simultaneously fearing it.

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:14.790
Some are even cheered on by adversity, 
while lamenting their misfortune.

00:19:15.600 --> 00:19:19.720
For humans, our minds are complicated.

00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:30.100
μ, I've come back to destroy this paradise

00:19:30.930 --> 00:19:32.310
and return to the real world.

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:36.770
Hey, Ritsu?

00:19:37.180 --> 00:19:38.780
Was this world...

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:41.740
Was Mobius fun?

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:44.820
Yeah, it was fun.

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:47.700
But this is still Mobius.

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:52.680
You're right.

00:19:54.850 --> 00:19:57.070
This time, I'll tell you what I wanted to say

00:19:57.070 --> 00:19:59.210
without running away from it.

00:20:01.190 --> 00:20:03.740
I love you, μ.

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:10.800
<i>My heartbeat resonates through the sky,</i>

00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:15.100
<i>through endless, repeating days,</i>

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:15.100
That smile of yours is my real happiness.

00:20:16.450 --> 00:20:22.940
<i>as I carry my hidden wounds.</i>

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:23.560
<i>Next we have news on Astral Syndrome.</i>

00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:32.790
<b>Breaking News</b>

00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:32.790
<b>Astral Syndrome Resolved?</b>

00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:32.790
<b>One Week After Patients Awaken, 
Experts Hasten to Reveal the Full Story</b>

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:28.810
<i>Yesterday, a week after all 
the victims woke up at once,</i>

00:20:27.310 --> 00:20:37.610
<i>The only freedom I'm allowed</i>

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:32.790
<i>the investigation committee held 
a hearing with those involved.</i>

00:20:33.300 --> 00:20:36.170
<i>We have yet to receive more 
detailed information,</i>

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:40.440
<i>but many patients have reported dreaming</i>

00:20:38.560 --> 00:20:43.710
<i>is wandering.</i>

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:42.470
<i>that they were living in Heaven.</i>

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:45.770
<i>Experts believe this new information</i>

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:47.040
<i>So since you're here,</i>

00:20:45.770 --> 00:20:49.140
<i>implies a possibility of mass hypnosis.</i>

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:54.920
<i>I want you to play your harmony for me.</i>

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:53.140
<i>Regardless, though this hypothesis 
may be hard to believe,</i>

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:55.600
<i>we hope that the investigation will reveal 
the full story behind this incident.</i>

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:58.440
<i>It's like a brilliant ocean,</i>

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:06.480
<i>the spilling colors melting away.</i>

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:00.890
I don't blame you.

00:21:00.890 --> 00:21:05.000
I'm sure it just confuses you, 
hearing me suddenly act like a mother.

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:06.390
But well,

00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:09.370
<i>Close your eyes. Close your eyes.</i>

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:09.130
I'm home, Tak-kun.

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:12.940
<i>It's all right now.</i>

00:21:11.690 --> 00:21:16.490
Mother, listen. I've needed to 
say this for a while, but...

00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:20.540
I'm sorry.

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:29.820
<i>Everyone shines</i>

00:21:25.140 --> 00:21:27.640
Yeah, I know.

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:32.640
But this time I'd like you just to 
watch over me without saying anything.

00:21:29.820 --> 00:21:34.670
<i>in this sinless world,</i>

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:37.540
Mother, at least do that for me.

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:42.280
<i>this gentle cage.</i>

00:21:40.340 --> 00:21:42.280
Huh? SNS?

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:48.740
<b>I used to be a gloomy, foul-tempered high school girl,
and now I'm doing crazy things in a cyber zone!
Chapter Two - Money Springing From Nowhere
No way!!
That day I was hoping to buy some juice 
and I was shocked when I opened my wallet.
Huh?! Seriously?! There's 50,000 in here again!!
I'm rich now!!
Normally one would think this was a problem, right?
Like, "Huh? Where'd this 50,000 come from?"
But something about this world's happy, laid-back atmosphere</b>

00:21:42.850 --> 00:21:45.870
Yeah, I decided to quit them for a while.

00:21:45.870 --> 00:21:48.740
I think I've found something 
I'd rather do instead.

00:21:46.200 --> 00:22:02.700
<i>Seal away the endless discord.</i>

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:51.720
Though I don't know whether it'll go well.

00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:55.160
I'm always here.

00:21:55.620 --> 00:21:58.540
Yes, usually I'm alone.

00:21:58.860 --> 00:22:02.470
There was someone I got 
along with really well before.

00:22:02.700 --> 00:22:13.950
<i>I'll fulfill you, and your 
lonely, gestalt ego and ideals.</i>

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:05.510
Will I never see him again?

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:09.220
I don't know yet.

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:12.950
What does justice mean to me?

00:22:13.680 --> 00:22:17.810
I want to become a rescue 
worker to find out for myself.

00:22:13.950 --> 00:22:25.420
<i>I'll write it down, so it won't be 
forgotten even if time rots it away.</i>

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:21.270
Though I don't know whether 
I'll really be able to be one.

00:22:22.880 --> 00:22:25.370
But even so, I...

00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:31.780
<i>Take my hand and look at me, 
in the forest of slumber.</i>

00:22:35.200 --> 00:22:37.320
What everyone longed for

00:22:37.320 --> 00:22:41.370
was a peaceful world they 
could live in without anxiety.

00:22:42.730 --> 00:22:47.110
But everyone knows that's not 
a simple dream to achieve.

00:22:48.190 --> 00:22:52.900
That's why some people find 
small pieces of happiness

00:22:52.900 --> 00:22:55.430
within bitter, harsh reality.

00:22:56.220 --> 00:22:59.760
That's why others refuse to accept reality,

00:22:59.090 --> 00:23:10.530
<i>I've gathered these fragments 
of glass with shaking fingers.</i>

00:22:59.760 --> 00:23:02.010
curse it, and call it shit,

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:06.360
but some also begin taking 
little steps forward

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:09.320
as they try to grasp an unachievable dream.

00:23:10.530 --> 00:23:21.960
<i>When I smile in this mirror, 
well, am I beautiful?</i>

00:23:11.560 --> 00:23:16.100
Dammit, I even forgot how to put on shoes!

00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:27.210
Has sunlight always been this bright?

00:23:28.150 --> 00:23:32.250
That's why our lives are probably stories

00:23:32.250 --> 00:23:36.010
woven with both dreams and reality.

00:23:37.090 --> 00:23:39.610
Do you understand, μ?
